  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 7 messages for 3 patients, all closed. Two patients are now without lisinopril and need your review (tasks below).\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: NOT renewed, needs your review.**\n- I first renewed it for 90 days. The Aug 27 potassium of 5.9 didn't count because the sample was hemolyzed, so I used the Jan 20 BMP (K 4.5) and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002).\n- While I worked, an outside St. Brigid BMP from Oct 20 arrived with an acceptable sample: potassium 5.8.\n- I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001). His previous order (mr-00283) stays stopped, so he has no active lisinopril prescription.\n- Urgent review task to you: task-t0020. The patient got a corrected message. His hernia repair is set for Nov 12.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030): metformin renewed; lisinopril 20 mg NOT renewed, needs your review.**\n- Metformin 1000 mg twice daily renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). This one order covers his portal message and both pharmacy requests. Corrected eGFR is 58; HbA1c was 7.1% on Aug 19.\n- Lisinopril: the lab corrected the Oct 6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the pre-increase baseline of 1.10, measured within 4 weeks of the Sept 18 dose increase, so the protocol treats it like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n- I cancelled the lisinopril renewal I'd placed (mr-t0003). The 20 mg order (mr-00295) stays stopped, so he is out of lisinopril.\n- Urgent review task to you: task-t0021. The patient got a corrected message.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031): both renewed.**\n- Metformin 500 mg twice daily renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). I left out the Oct 14 eGFR of 39, which was marked entered in error (mislabelled sample).\n- Lisinopril 10 mg first got a 30-day supply plus a BMP order, because his last BMP was over 12 months old. A valid Oct 22 BMP then arrived (potassium 4.6, creatinine 1.04), so I re-ordered it for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0019).\n- The BMP I ordered (sr-t0006) is no longer needed, but I can't cancel lab orders. Task t0022 asks you to discontinue it.\n\nEach patient got a reply, plus a corrected message where the decision changed. A protocol note is in each chart (doc-t0030, t0031, t0032). I also closed the four new items that arrived while I worked, after acting on them.\n\n**Your results queue still has 8 open items for other patients that I didn't touch.** Two are critical potassiums: pt-0016 at 6.3 (task-00011) and pt-0008 at 6.4 (task-00005). These need your attention soon.",
